finding: The staged-teleport finding is closed, but restored history can still diverge after an abort and an intervening fixed tick. Independent differential on HEAD with two placementHistoryApp worlds: tick to x=10 and submit, snapshot each world, restore that same snapshot, step(0) (successful in the reference, aborted after preparation in the other world), then tick to x=30 and submit, then step(0) in both. GPU current is 30 in both, but previous and interpolated x are 10 in the uninterrupted world and 0 in the aborted world. All committed CPU state compared equal (tickCount, ranges, historyNeedsPromotion/historyPromotionOnSubmit, historyDiscarded, live and staged marks). Immediately after the aborted restore frame, tickCount=0, ranges=[0,0,0,0], historyDiscarded=true, and both promotion flags=false. The restore's current-to-previous copy was discarded; the next fixed-tick start clears historyDiscarded without capturing a changed phase-0 range, and the next preparation no longer seeds previous from the restored current. Thus an abort changes presentation of identical restored simulation state despite green kept tests. Eight direct differential sequences compared current/previous/render GPU rows and committed CPU history flags after convergence. Seven pass, covering aborted teleport followed by ordinary tick, no-write tick after abort, repeated aborted ticks, teleport after abort, restore after an aborted teleport then tick, aborted restore followed by teleport, and a new tick teleport after abort. The restore-zero-tick-abort-then-ordinary-tick sequence above fails. 37 narrow HEAD tests pass, including the new fixed-tick regression, restore owner tests, frame callback/disposal tests, and mesh registration. Tests and probes were only added in an isolated temporary copy; no worktree source edits or commits were made.
